wKqZdGW0giaPlbzQdhHo_--k7RlJ-mHLwZ5Ilq9rGzXgGpsxDGav2o4PmlU_P83i5T7Wn1Kl7gd3xifH5YYFtQAuKgCyGEMU9a_XWCLrLqzQGRtkAHKog4QcRDdVHen0RhuWL6Fv2TSE9khaa-qbS4yX_NVKG3f9GfZmLEb6KpTvibBBNm3T3mXt5RKt7Nt2fko-jBuOtvm44ndOuES543B7m1-fLIZotRiC33SzlGmg1QfmTBPnyOL7LO4LoLGAK30LMXkoxlhL4Tv7d7CPRnhLRNGF4F4w2dVJDuwnQPLMuy23Nz4uqoz4IEG"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0923f0c6632b26ea016adb6d4e57788191a54e5f39a56fcf31","call_id":"call_b9fab80eff974cf6bd7ffcc5a74baad6","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The contextual reading is exact: under parameters n,E and H001 (nonempty), H002 (compact), P states dim_H(E×[0,1])=dim_H(E)+1, matching frozen-target.md and spec.full_target; the conclusion need not repeat these contextual assumptions. n=0 and empty-set convention are explicitly addressed. However, the supplied proof does not establish its target: S002 asserts without adequate derivation that divergence of scale contents as δ tends to zero yields Hausdorff measure equal to top; M008's supremum formula alone does not justify that step as written, and the needed quantifier/unboundedness argument is absent. There are also unproved key covering estimates and constructions in S001/S002. Thus target-edge proof closure fails.\",\"locations\":[\"frozen-target.md:7-17\",\"problem.md:3\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"spec.json:/conclusion\",\"spec.json:/parameters\",\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/2 (P)\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{\"D001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The sole global definition identifies volume as pinned Lebesgue measure on the usual real line. It has no binders, dependencies, or prerequisites; it asserts no theorem/property beyond identifying the object. Use with restricted measure is distinguishable from volume itself.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/0\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/definitions/0\"]}},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official pinned HausdorffDimension source lines 114-118 prove the stated lower-exponent infinite-measure result. Full-signature evidence matches: implicit EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace, BorelSpace, set and NNReal exponent; theorem conclusion is ↑d<dimH(s) → Hausdorff measure=⊤. Application at S002 uses s<D and NNReal coercion, in a Euclidean Borel space.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:94-118\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The supplied probe reports the complete outer telescope and theorem, with Countable β and each summand AEMeasurable. S002 supplies a substantive measurable-indicator argument and application mapping. The pinned official declaration body was not inspected, so source fidelity is not fully audited.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"]},\"M003\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Pinned source is HausdorffDimension.lean, whose module documentation states the zero-measure-above-dimension property (lines 15-20); supplied full signature agrees, including all implicit structures. The S001 application uses exponent q>D in Euclidean Borel space.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M003/0/sources/M003\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:15-20\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/2\"]},\"M004\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official source module overview explicitly says Lipschitz maps do not increase Hausdorff dimension (HausdorffDimension.lean:44-52); supplied complete signature matches the two EMetricSpace instances, NNReal K, Lipschitz premise, and image inequality. S003 gives the ambient projection and verifies its Lipschitz bound and image using nonemptiness.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M004/0/sources/M004\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:44-52\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/3\"]},\"M005\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The official source module documents Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior for finite-dimensional real vector spaces (HausdorffDimension.lean:54-57). Probe signature correctly includes normed additive commutative group, real normed space, finite-dimensionality and nonempty interior. The interval application checks these conditions.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M005/0/sources/M005\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:54-57\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/4\"]},\"M008\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The pinned official Hausdorff.lean:23-27 gives the exact positive-scale supremum / Nat-cover infimum formula; lines 61-65 explain the nonempty-set summand convention. The probe signature agrees with outer structures and full formula. Applications use the formula in both ambient Euclidean spaces; not all mathematical consequences asserted from it are thereby established.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M008/0/sources/M008\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Hausdorff.lean:23-27\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Hausdorff.lean:61-65\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/5\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/11\"]},\"M009\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Probe evidence gives the full theorem telescope including measurable space, measure, implicit ENNReal functions, and pointwise inequality. Actual official declaration source was not inspected; application is identified at S002.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M009/0/sources/M009\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/6\"]},\"M010\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Probe gives the full measurable-set premise and ENNReal constant conclusion, matching the restatement. Official declaration body was not inspected. S002 explains measurability and the restricted measure application.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M010/0/sources/M010\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/7\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/14\"]},\"M011\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The provided signature is for Real.volume_Icc with arbitrary real endpoints and entails ENNReal.ofReal(right-left), including reversed endpoints. Official source was not inspected. In-use applications concern interval lengths and total mass.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/10/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/8\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/12\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M011 (not in retrieved range)\"]},\"M012\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Provided complete signature states non-top Hausdorff measure implies dimH≤↑d with all three ambient structures. Actual official source was not inspected; two S001 applications are recorded.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/11/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/13\"]},\"M013\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Provided full signature includes generic outer-measure-class and FunLike instance conditions and subset premise. Source declaration body not inspected; S002's use identifies volume and set inclusion but full source verification remains outstanding.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/12/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/10\"]},\"M014\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"Provided full signature has EMetricSpace, measurable and Borel structures, Hausdorff measure=top premise and conclusion ↑d≤dimH. Actual official source was not inspected; application is recorded in S002.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/13/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/13\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The visible graph has H001/H002 roots, retained M-source nodes, one R001 producer for P and a single output P; every direct source is listed in R001. No extra hypothesis is added. This is a structural inspection only; mathematical AND-closure fails because the sole inference is not established. No per-inference packet replay is claimed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"FAIL\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"finding\":\"The conclusion that unbounded scale contents as δ tends to zero imply Hausdorff measure at exponent s+1 equals ⊤ is asserted without the necessary quantified argument. The M008 supremum-over-scales formula is not, by itself, a proof of this conclusion: the required assertion that for each finite K a positive-scale content exceeds K (and then the supremum is top) must be established. This blocks the lower-bound branch and target closure.\"},{\"severity\":\"FAIL\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"finding\":\"The grid-cover estimate and the associated dimension upper-bound argument are only sketched: the claimed C h^(−n) count for a bounding box, the countable cover/cost construction, and the passage from vanishing measure to D≤n by taking an infimum are not fully justified in the declared logical/calculation inputs. For n=0 a separate interval argument is given, but the text also makes an overbroad all-n grid assertion that requires handling separately.\"},{\"severity\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"location\":\"signature-evidence.json; source lines cited in source_reviews\",\"finding\":\"Full official source inspection through read_mathlib is incomplete for M002, M009-M014. Their probe records are evidence of signatures, not substitutes for direct official source review.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","